# Downloaded imaging data is never committed.
#
# The DWI volumes are tens of megabytes each and are reproducible from
# `download.sh` plus the OpenNeuro S3 objects it documents, so the provenance
# belongs in git and the bytes do not. Committing one is effectively permanent:
# git keeps the blob in history even after a later deletion.
#
# `README.md` and `download.sh` are the tracked contents of this directory.
*.nii
*.nii.gz

# Gradient sidecars come with the volumes and are re-fetched the same way.
*.bval
*.bvec
*.json

# DataLad/git-annex working clones created by `download.sh`.
ds*_repo/
